1.1.1-snapshot
  A Development page with a reset, and clearer volume settings
    The volume settings now sit on a General page, and a new Development page holds the debug log and a reset to defaults.
    The new pages move where MCM stores each setting. Open Development after the update and reset every setting.

  - Added a Development page with the debug log and a button that resets every setting to its default.
  - Changed the volume and pause labels to show their unit, and added a tooltip to each setting.
  - Fixed the guitar text, which named the campfire guitar where the mod controls the guitar you play.

1.1.0
  The DiegeticControl name, a new MCM banner and the xlibs 1.9.0 floor
    AlifeDiegetic is now DiegeticControl, part of the Diegetic sound family, with a new MCM banner and a separate diegeticcontrol.log.
    From this release the mod needs xlibs 1.9.0 or newer.

  - Changed the mod name to DiegeticControl in the MCM, the banner and the log, which is now diegeticcontrol.log.
  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.9.0.

1.0.9
  The AlifeDiegetic name, steady radio volume, and the modded exes check
    Diegetic Audio Control is now AlifeDiegetic. Radio and megaphone volume holds at the level you set, and the MCM footer shows the platform status.
    The load check now stops the game with a message when the modded exes are missing or too old, and when xlibs is older than 1.8.4.

  - Changed the mod name to AlifeDiegetic in the MCM and the log, which is now alifediegetic.log.
  - Fixed radio and megaphone volume drifting from the level you set. A frequency slider back at its default restores the original timing.
  - Fixed the volume slider and toggle labels, which now show in English and Russian.
  - Added the modded exes check. The game stops at load with a message when it finds neither demonized 20250908 or newer nor AOEngine.
  - Added the platform status to the MCM footer and the log. It names the exe build and how much of the mod that build supports.
  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.8.4.

1.0.8
  The xlibs 1.3.0 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.3.0, on vanilla Anomaly 1.5.3 as well as on the modded exes.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.3.0.

1.0.7
  The xlibs 1.2.5 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.5, and the load check accepts any newer compatible version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.5.

1.0.6
  A timer fix, the MCM banner and the Russian MCM restored
    The radio and megaphone timers work in modpacks that replace the vanilla timer queue, and the Russian MCM reads correctly again.
    A banner and the mod version now sit on the MCM, and the log names the mod and xlibs versions at startup.

  - Fixed the timers in modpacks that replace the vanilla timer queue, such as demonized time events.
  - Fixed the Russian MCM text, which showed broken characters. The file is back in windows-1251.
  - Fixed the xlibs check calling an xlibs function that no longer exists.
  - Added the MCM banner and the mod version, and the mod and xlibs versions to the log at startup.

1.0.5
  The xlibs 1.2.3 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.3, and the load check accepts any newer compatible version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.3.

1.0.4
  The xlibs 1.2.1 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.1, and the load check asks for that exact version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.1.

1.0.3
  The MCM reset button and faster settings reads
    The MCM reset button now restores every setting, and the mod reads its settings from a snapshot.

  - Added support for the MCM reset button.
  - Improved settings performance. The mod reads a snapshot of the MCM values in place of a query per sound.
  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.0.

1.0.2
  An exact xlibs version check
    The load check now matches the xlibs version exactly, where it used to compare the version as text.

  - Fixed the xlibs check comparing versions as text. It now asks for the exact version.

1.0.1
  The xlibs check and the Russian translation
    From this release the mod checks the xlibs version at load, and the MCM reads in Russian.

  - Added the xlibs check at load, with a message when xlibs is missing or outdated.
  - Added the Russian translation.

1.0.0
  Volume and pause control for radios, megaphones, the guitar and the harmonica
    The first release sets how loud each in-world source plays, and how often radios and megaphones speak.

  - Added a volume slider for each source, under a master volume.
  - Added a frequency slider for radios and megaphones, which stretches or shortens the pause between their broadcasts.
  - Added a toggle for each source.
  - Added a quiet fallback when the guitar or the harmonica mod is missing.
